afa451d266383e0566a916bfbe5f68\", \"size_bytes\": 15348, \"source\": {\"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\", \"object\": null, \"path\": \"codex/HISTORY.json\", \"root\": \"successor\", \"selector\": null, \"sha256\": \"21c30f02798ae39e60d89bba6f3489eb73afa451d266383e0566a916bfbe5f68\"}}}, \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.response/1\", \"status\": \"ok\"}\n{\"evidence\": {\"id\": \"sha256:0b98429411f9ae3ed55efcc3db6acc5a96ff4647aa5876de7fb4cfcfb9dcf2e6\", \"sha256\": \"0b98429411f9ae3ed55efcc3db6acc5a96ff4647aa5876de7fb4cfcfb9dcf2e6\"}, \"id\": \"codex-s1-read-10\", \"operation\": \"source.read\", \"operation_outcome\": {\"cause\": \"declared output available\", \"core_value\": \"satisfied\", \"evidence\": [], \"limits\": [\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"], \"predicate\": \"B(source.read)[request_sha256=2e9fd31801487ec615eae0c2e4bb31801fda9d01a64331c661dcd23453c0db42]: declared output availability\", \"source_parent\": {\"clause\": \"results\", \"member\": \"FOUNDATIONS.md\", \"sha256\": \"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"}, \"value\": \"returned\"}, \"refusal\": null, \"result\": {\"artifact\": null, \"value\": {\"acquisition\": {}, \"content\": \"### Transition evidence\\n\\nA reviewable transition identifies the exact candidate, the affected\\nrelations, the changed realisation paths, the authority paths added or\\nremoved, the retained and open seams, the focused proof, any required\\nintegration proof, the explicit non-changes, and, where an assessor was\\nactivated, the assessor's recommended disposition, with the decision\\nowner's disposition beside it once one is made (\\u00a73). Consumers\\nchoose the representation. Transition evidence is a read\\nmodel; it does not become specification, design or admission authority\\n(P6, P4b).\\n\\nConstruction uses the cheapest focused proof capable of falsifying the\\nactive relation. Expensive whole-candidate qualification occurs at a\\ndeclared candidate boundary rather than after every local edit, unless the\\naffected risk makes whole-candidate proof necessary (\\u00a76). A durable or\\nreconstructable authority claim is not established solely by a same-process\\nproof when loss of incidental process state is a material counterexample:\\nthe proof destroys or excludes the incidental authority and compares the\\n\", \"coordinates\": {\"lines\": [1750, 1768]}, \"encoding\": \"utf8\", \"parent_sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\", \"selected_sha256\": \"08d23dd3949b21b80e23fa46bffedff55bfa456a51e1afd8df831b5f13bbd216\", \"size_bytes\": 1090, \"source\": {\"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\", \"object\": null, \"path\": \"standards/ACTIVATION.md\", \"root\": \"method\", \"selector\": {\"lines\": [1750, 1768]}, \"sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}}, \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.response/1\", \"status\": \"ok\"}\n{\"evidence\": {\"id\": \"sha256:0d3b895c495c1c1b1c12389e160ed8294c9e843ca7eaa6ccb81ae62476148f29\", \"sha256\": \"0d3b895c495c1c1b1c12389e160ed8294c9e843ca7eaa6ccb81ae62476148f29\"}, \"id\": \"codex-s1-read-11\", \"operation\": \"source.read\", \"operation_outcome\": {\"cause\": \"declared output available\", \"core_value\": \"satisfied\", \"evidence\": [], \"limits\": [\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"], \"predicate\": \"B(source.read)[request_sha256=4600b77959b8fabc89f5e5a33d3cc66bd612bc94b84683fd569ec1afb3195846]: declared output availability\", \"source_parent\": {\"clause\": \"results\", \"member\": \"FOUNDATIONS.md\", \"sha256\": \"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"}, \"value\": \"returned\"}, \"refusal\": null, \"result\": {\"artifact\": null, \"value\": {\"acquisition\": {}, \"content\": \"A step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS \\u00a73, P0): the\\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\\nexists (P5, P6):\\n\\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\\n\\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\\n\\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS \\u00a74 Results).\\n\\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \\\"a candidate is available\\\", never\\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (\\u00a75) carries it as a\\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\\n(FOUNDATIONS \\u00a74 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\\n(P5, P6).\\n\\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\\n(P6).\\n\\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS \\u00a74 Results, Refinements). A stop\\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\\nP3).\\n\\n### Disposition\\n\\nThe decision owner disposes an assessed candidate with one of four\\nsemantic dispositions (\\u00a71, Roles and delegation; P6, P5). An assessor may recommend one; the\\nrecommendation is evidence for the decision owner, never a disposition\\n([EVALUATION \\u00a74](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results)). The disposition is the\\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\\n\", \"coordinates\": {\"lines\": [1004, 1055]}, \"encoding\": \"utf8\", \"parent_sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\", \"selected_sha256\": \"503cf7de07bd21bd57279b2e6bae3b29db70ad3cc24a169474656475c39cefd8\", \"size_bytes\": 3256, \"source\": {\"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\", \"object\": null, \"path\": \"standards/ACTIVATION.md\", \"root\": \"method\", \"selector\": {\"lines\": [1004, 1055]}, \"sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}}, \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.response/1\", \"status\": \"ok\"}\n{\"evidence\": {\"id\": \"sha256:8f40aec0ac5042f3d9e99896b07d6eeee534a8defb8b0929f4b46d58e169124c\", \"sha256\": \"8f40aec0ac5042f3d9e99896b07d6eeee534a8defb8b0929f4b46d58e169124c\"}, \"id\": \"codex-s1-read-12\", \"operation\": \"source.read\", \"operation_outcome\": {\"cause\": \"declared output available\", \"core_value\": \"satisfied\", \"evidence\": [], \"limits\": [\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"], \"predicate\": \"B(source.read)[request_sha256=6390d13776b4729c57f541dfd729746c3adcb2ee6cc3ab1e51b034563ae24907]: declared output availability\", \"source_parent\": {\"clause\": \"results\", \"member\": \"FOUNDATIONS.md\", \"sha256\": \"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"}, \"value\": \"returned\"}, \"refusal\": null, \"result\": {\"artifact\": null, \"value\": {\"acquisition\": {}, \"content\": \"# Codex tenant design \\u2014 T001 candidate 1\\n\\nRecorded before implementation. Scope: build_tenants/codex only; construction authority is operator codex/TASK.md SHA256 eae576ac13cbf358889845b6532c62482d0cc593d9c669eb467a88911d01a9e0, grant urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:1. No Product acceptance, publication or installation is claimed.\\n\\n## Basis and source ownership\\n\\nSTDO Skills common inventory a6d348b8385ea453ce29362fb9d74559304b1b91743b3c9ea31a83a9f02b5f2d governs this candidate. STDO stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/ manifest 60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8 owns the method. Its installed basis was verified by stdo status --definition stdo_skills.json --verify on 2026-10-25. The discovery channel does not select a newer basis.\\n\\nRequirements SHA256 dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc and scenarios SHA256 089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e remain common external authority. The frame basis SHA256 00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa is selected by this activation for construction, not accepted by this Worker. Method routing comes from specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md SHA256 15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3. Installed deciding sections are acquired as needed; no copied methodology is installed.\\n\\n## Algorithm and host binding\\n\\nOne skill, stdo-work, supplies task-based discovery for an already governed workspace and explicit setup requests. Its name and description remain available to Codex; automatic invocation stays enabled by omitting any disabling policy. Only the entrypoint and the relevant reference are acquired. References are packaged inside the skill, so copying the complete directory preserves their links.\\n\\n| Requirements | Algorithm | Codex or tool mechanism | Finite proof |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| SK-01 | Route relevant task, ignore unrelated task, distinguish discovery from execution | SKILL.md frontmatter; repository .agents/skills/stdo-work; explicit $stdo-work | Q01, Q02, Q12 |\\n| SK-02 | Select one Product, verify exact installed basis, acquire bootstrap and deciding owner | stdo status --definition PATH --verify; public source.read with exact SourceRefs | Q03 |\\n| SK-03 | Reuse sufficient authority; choose direct Writer for a sufficient small effect; coordinate only on material boundary | Codex reasoning over acquired contract; host actors only where selected and admitted | Q04, Q05 |\\n| SK-04 | Discover exact schemas, call required operation, retain actual response and effect evidence | native a_c public MCP or explicitly configured CLI using complete request envelopes | Q01, Q06, Q08 |\\n| SK-05 | Preserve smallest deciding causal context including retained obligations and differing histories | exact SourceRefs, context.assemble when selected; activation carrier | Q05, Q07 |\\n| SK-06 | Bind child outcome, basis, territory, proof, consumer and stop; consume closed return before next activation | configured contract.preflight, dispatch.start/observe and return.capture/check where admitted; no invented tool | Q04, Q05 |\\n| SK-07 | Derive expected behavior from source before exact candidate; retain exposure and family limits | review.prepare where selected; fresh separately admitted reviewer; source.read | Q05, Q09 |\\n| SK-08 | Reacquire current evidence, reconcile uncertain effects before retry, retain unaffected evidence | workspace.observe, source.read, evidence.read, granted recovery path | Q07-Q10 |\\n| SK-09 | Separate candidate availability, assessment, consumer disposition, acceptance | declared closed return schema, original basis, explicit residuals and not_performed | Q06, Q09, Q10 |\\n| SK-10 | Prepare exact immutable candidate; act only on authorized release destination; scoped package install/update/remove | selected release tool discovered from its contract; file-copy deployment only with corresponding grant | Q11, Q12 |\\n| SK-11 | Package references together; inventory exact content; retain previous identity on update | read-only package verifier; owned-directory installation recipe | Q12 |\\n| SK-12 | Freeze substantive tasks and independent oracle, preserve every attempt and unknown costs | qualification plan and actual host traces, not keyword success grading | Q01-Q12 |\\n\\nCodex mechanics are independently sourced in operator codex/HOST.md SHA256 6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e: codex-cli 0.164.0, repository-local .agents/skills discovery, explicit $skill-name, relative references, restart when discovery is stale. Configured model/effort gpt-6-astra/max is inherited; actual resolution is unknown unless the run records it. No nested actor is launched in this construction.\\n\\n## Tool boundary and failure behavior\\n\\nNative method profile urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1 SHA256 a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7 is selected. tools.describe reports provisional construction support, not qualification. Its builder identity v2.5.1-rc.2 is distinct from this selected operation binding. There is no supported native results.conjoin. Executive consumption is F_P under its granted relation; any decision must preserve required predicates, applicability, incompatible bases and unresolved contradictions.\\n\\nHost reads, SHA256 computation and static package checks are declared auxiliary mechanics. They establish byte/structure facts only and never replace required source.read, workspace.observe, work.write, admission or assessment results. All current construction deliverables are written with work.write, own observation and exact preimage; postimage and OperationEvidence are then read. Unknown completion stops dependent writing pending reconciliation.\\n\\nA failed required operation withholds its dependent claim. Independent work can continue under its existing grant. No automatic retries, authorization renewal or publication follow from successful transport. A missing installation or ambiguous Product is a basis problem, not a request to adopt latest. An unperformed assessment has no core result; performed inconclusive assessment is indeterminate; construction without an output is incomplete for candidate availability.\\n\\n## Installation and qualification\\n\\nREADME supplies a repository-local, single-directory copy recipe and explicit update/removal custody checks. No installer mutates host configuration implicitly. A read-only verifier checks packaged resources and optional observed inventory. It does not assess instruction semantics or host discovery.\\n\\nQ01-Q12 actual host trials, source-first independent assessment, release and owner acceptance remain unperformed here. The qualification plan keeps each case/lane visible and preserves failures. Static checks support only packaging integrity; they do not justify automatic-selection reliability or efficiency claims.\\n\", \"coordinates\": null, \"encoding\": \"utf8\", \"parent_sha256\": \"3364d66e885f7a8b66bf6a9b2fc903b606ff7fdeacbaba4aabc5fc6f2d6f9df6\", \"selected_sha256\": \"3364d66e885f7a8b66bf6a9b2fc903b606ff7fdeacbaba4aabc5fc6f2d6f9df6\", \"size_bytes\": 6911, \"source\": {\"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\", \"object\": null, \"path\": \"codex/PRIOR-PROPOSAL.md\", \"root\": \"successor\", \"selector\": null, \"sha256\": \"3364d66e885f7a8b66bf6a9b2fc903b606ff7fdeacbaba4aabc5fc6f2d6f9df6\"}}}, \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.response/1\", \"status\": \"ok\"}\n{\"evidence\": {\"id\": \"sha256:320af0af67100f305bc2bf31a47e5725254d69ca019aa01e9e39de86f71c40ab\", \"sha256\": \"320af0af67100f305bc2bf31a47e5725254d69ca019aa01e9e39de86f71c40ab\"}, \"id\": \"codex-s1-read-13\", \"operation\": \"source.read\", \"operation_outcome\": {\"cause\": \"declared output available\", \"core_value\": \"satisfied\", \"evidence\": [], \"limits\": [\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"], \"predicate\": \"B(source.read)[request_sha256=9eb96c177b034b485e50ad3e13b010d602b3ba6a9b85aa4af2e43ba5872876ec]: declared output availability\", \"source_parent\": {\"clause\": \"results\", \"member\": \"FOUNDATIONS.md\", \"sha256\": \"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"}, \"value\": \"returned\"}, \"refusal\": null, \"result\": {\"artifact\": null, \"value\": {\"acquisition\": {}, \"content\": \"{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"a_c.fd-support.method-binding/1\\\",\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"bounded-native-binding-candidate\\\",\\n  \\\"method\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"STDO3.0.1 RC1\\\",\\n    \\\"uri\\\": \\\"stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/\\\",\\n    \\\"manifest_sha256\\\": \\\"60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8\\\",\\n    \\\"source_commit\\\": \\\"fe4941f56a52ed3697a2b516d8d68948b0ea65d9\\\",\\n    \\\"package\\\": \\\"specification_methodology/v3/\\\",\\n    \\\"selected_profiles\\\": [\\n      \\\"EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"builder\\\": {\\n    \\\"uri\\\": \\\"stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/\\\",\\n    \\\"manifest_sha256\\\": \\\"3d860ff4c1746f06ac25295a9e205cffb8e7725869615ac77cf2304b70ff2782\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"members\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"member\\\": \\\"REFERENCE_FRAME.md\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"8152838639950b09389f99181172792100e4470b4807b4e112870cd4e6f6ba21\\\",\\n      \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n        \\\"11-the-activation-packet\\\",\\n        \\\"13-minimal-declarations\\\",\\n        \\\"rf-016-implementation-neutrality\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"member\\\": \\\"ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\n      \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n        \\\"intake\\\",\\n        \\\"admission\\\",\\n        \\\"3-step-results-and-disposition\\\",\\n        \\\"7-closed-result-and-reuse\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"member\\\": \\\"FOUNDATIONS.md\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\\\",\\n      \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n        \\\"results\\\",\\n        \\\"assertions-and-observation\\\",\\n        \\\"change-impact-and-evidence-reuse\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"member\\\": \\\"EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"fcef434630e270d216f494de97ee727ad46690db89a4b73edac4b88ff921c62e\\\",\\n      \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n        \\\"19-baseline-specific-basis-and-activation-additions\\\",\\n        \\\"no-mutation-while-executive\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"member\\\": \\\"AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"b39c45fd86b8f9add7d196b2974a8e5f75bf4a327cf796e362716a6b4f5776d5\\\",\\n      \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n        \\\"5-traversals-and-functor-kinds\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"member\\\": \\\"EVALUATION.md\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"478fd21feda72d64e62a92f970b37bade3f9aadfb17c73649cdb1a7866581eff\\\",\\n      \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n        \\\"3-independent-assessment\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"member\\\": \\\"SPEC_METHOD.md\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"b2773dc0c9feb429b6b357bcfd60e7df46e54db8adcb04dc8d6dbfa023b73677\\\",\\n      \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n        \\\"11-build-tenant-binding\\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"carrier\\\": \\\"Existing a_c.fd-support /1 carriers; this profile supplies the native semantic binding, not new method law.\\\",\\n  \\\"mapping\\\": {\\n    \\\"packet\\\": \\\"REFERENCE_FRAME section11; existing groups preserve required native coordinates. Native intake outcome/admission/shared machinery are supplied as exact sources in packet relations and grant.\\\",\\n    \\\"admission\\\": \\\"ACTIVATION Admission; existing Product-located mechanism and exact contract evidence remain necessary; profile selection supplies no grant.\\\",\\n    \\\"work_result\\\": \\\"ACTIVATION Construction availability: candidate_ready/satisfied, incomplete/falsified, refused/falsified, re_entry_requested cause determines out_of_frame or invalid_basis; no assessment manufactured.\\\",\\n    \\\"return\\\": \\\"ACTIVATION section7; original evaluations/not_performed/residuals/invalidators remain distinct, and currentness is consumer-relative.\\\",\\n    \\\"operation_outcome\\\": \\\"B(op) is output/effect-evidence payload availability, not physical completion, semantic success or admission. Existing cause-tagged mapping is retained under native FOUNDATIONS Results.\\\",\\n    \\\"classification\\\": \\\"Named read, render, launch and write operations are not universally classified F_D; pure finite declared predicate checks retain their narrow evidence claim. External execution and F_P meaning remain separate.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"unsupported\\\": [\\n    \\\"results.conjoin: no native operator qualification\\\",\\n    \\\"arbitrary method profiles or translations\\\",\\n    \\\"semantic context sufficiency certification\\\",\\n    \\\"universal F_D classification or full calculus conformance\\\",\\n    \\\"OS sandboxing or actor/provider qualification\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\", \"coordinates\": null, \"encoding\": \"utf8\", \"parent_sha256\": \"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\", \"selected_sha256\": \"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\", \"size_bytes\": 3988, \"source\": {\"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\", \"object\": null, \"path\": \"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json\", \"root\": \"tool\", \"selector\": null, \"sha256\": \"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\"}}}, \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.response/1\", \"status\": \"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nargv=json.loads(\\\"[\\\\\\\"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-B\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--policy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/successor-1/codex/worker-policy.json\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--policy-sha256\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"038f1b1fdd56d0860dbfc94a0a17ff28e98e41153f6774cf4dc5ff7658d425b9\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--principal\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"codex\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--request\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\"]\\\")\nreq={\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-s1-contract-focus\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"tools.describe\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{}}\nr=json.loads(subprocess.run(argv,input=json.dumps(req),text=True,capture_output=True).stdout)\nv=r[\\\"result\\\"][\\\"value\\\"]\nprint(\\\"top keys\\\",list(v))\nprint(\\\"operations\\\",json.dumps(v.get(\\\"operations\\\",{})))\nfor k in [\\\"WorkWriteArguments\\\",\\\"WorkspaceObserveArguments\\\",\\\"ClosedReturn\\\",\\\"WorkResult\\\",\\\"Evaluation\\\",\\\"Residual\\\",\\\"NotPerformed\\\",\\\"WorkGrant\\\"]:\n if k in v.get(\\\"content_schemas\\\",{}).get(\\\"\"'$defs\",{}): print(k,json.dumps(v[\"content_schemas\"][\"$defs\"][k]))\nprint(\"other schemas\",json.dumps({k:v[k] for k in v if k not in [\"content_schemas\",\"operations\"]}))\n\nPY'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
