{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json, subprocess, pathlib, hashlib, sys, time\nargv=json.loads(\\\"[\\\\\\\"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-B\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--policy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/successor-1/codex/worker-policy.json\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--policy-sha256\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"038f1b1fdd56d0860dbfc94a0a17ff28e98e41153f6774cf4dc5ff7658d425b9\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--principal\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"codex\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--request\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\"]\\\")\ntask=json.loads(\\\"{\\\\\\\"engine\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"root\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"successor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"codex/TASK.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"sha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"4c33deea408deef15ac9900f66d5986b06efefb94de40697cf249d536770845b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"selector\\\\\\\":null}\\\")\nroot=pathlib.Path(\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills\\\")\ndef call(op,args,rid):\n r=subprocess.run(argv,input=json.dumps({\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":rid,\\\"operation\\\":op,\\\"arguments\\\":args}),text=True,capture_output=True)\n if r.returncode or r.stderr:\n  print(json.dumps({\\\"transport_exit\\\":r.returncode,\\\"stderr\\\":r.stderr}),flush=True)\n result=json.loads(r.stdout)\n if result[\\\"status\\\"]\"'!=\"ok\":\n  print(json.dumps(result),flush=True); raise SystemExit(\"Required public operation failed; no retry\")\n return result\n\nr=call(\"workspace.observe\",{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"build_tenants/codex/README.md\",\"kind\":\"file\"},{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"build_tenants/codex/tests/verify_package.py\",\"kind\":\"file\"}]},\"codex-s1-support-reconcile\")\nprint(json.dumps(r))\n\nPY'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json, subprocess, pathlib, hashlib, sys, time\nargv=json.loads(\\\"[\\\\\\\"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-B\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--policy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/successor-1/codex/worker-policy.json\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--policy-sha256\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"038f1b1fdd56d0860dbfc94a0a17ff28e98e41153f6774cf4dc5ff7658d425b9\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--principal\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"codex\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--request\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\"]\\\")\ntask=json.loads(\\\"{\\\\\\\"engine\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"root\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"successor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"codex/TASK.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"sha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"4c33deea408deef15ac9900f66d5986b06efefb94de40697cf249d536770845b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"selector\\\\\\\":null}\\\")\nroot=pathlib.Path(\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills\\\")\ndef call(op,args,rid):\n r=subprocess.run(argv,input=json.dumps({\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":rid,\\\"operation\\\":op,\\\"arguments\\\":args}),text=True,capture_output=True)\n if r.returncode or r.stderr:\n  print(json.dumps({\\\"transport_exit\\\":r.returncode,\\\"stderr\\\":r.stderr}),flush=True)\n result=json.loads(r.stdout)\n if result[\\\"status\\\"]\"'!=\"ok\":\n  print(json.dumps(result),flush=True); raise SystemExit(\"Required public operation failed; no retry\")\n return result\n\nr=call(\"workspace.observe\",{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"build_tenants/codex/README.md\",\"kind\":\"file\"},{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"build_tenants/codex/tests/verify_package.py\",\"kind\":\"file\"}]},\"codex-s1-support-reconcile\")\nprint(json.dumps(r))\n\nPY'","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\": {\"id\": \"sha256:c2954208a85312152038de424fe52690e883fbe74d7534d0addd5eb76a9f13e7\", \"sha256\": \"c2954208a85312152038de424fe52690e883fbe74d7534d0addd5eb76a9f13e7\"}, \"id\": \"codex-s1-support-reconcile\", \"operation\": \"workspace.observe\", \"operation_outcome\": {\"cause\": \"declared output available\", \"core_value\": \"satisfied\", \"evidence\": [], \"limits\": [\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"], \"predicate\": \"B(workspace.observe)[request_sha256=ed3c1889fc9a00fa71e16612b7cf21a203bcd73df0d281273830ae26c16229d1]: declared output availability\", \"source_parent\": {\"clause\": \"results\", \"member\": \"FOUNDATIONS.md\", \"sha256\": \"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"}, \"value\": \"returned\"}, \"refusal\": null, \"result\": {\"artifact\": {\"id\": \"sha256:da84510a7bffb78cfcadb9ad890380b767401db969e7f65f25c662ff48d32ec4\", \"sha256\": \"da84510a7bffb78cfcadb9ad890380b767401db969e7f65f25c662ff48d32ec4\"}, \"value\": {\"bindings\": {\"method_profile\": {\"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\", \"object\": null, \"path\": \"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json\", \"root\": \"tool\", \"selector\": null, \"sha256\": \"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\"}, \"policy_sha256\": \"038f1b1fdd56d0860dbfc94a0a17ff28e98e41153f6774cf4dc5ff7658d425b9\", \"product_definition\": {\"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\", \"object\": null, \"path\": \"stdo_skills.json\", \"root\": \"product\", \"selector\": null, \"sha256\": \"4339a7dbc735052c08962154966fc13a4e30206d42ba2e80b53c6009a5008c22\"}}, \"diff\": [], \"entries\": [{\"exists\": false, \"path\": \"build_tenants/codex/README.md\", \"root\": \"product\", \"sha256\": null, \"size\": null, \"type\": \"absent\"}, {\"exists\": false, \"path\": \"build_tenants/codex/tests/verify_package.py\", \"root\": \"product\", \"sha256\": null, \"size\": null, \"type\": \"absent\"}], \"gaps\": [], \"git\": null, \"observed_interval\": {\"clock\": \"unix_ns\", \"ended_ns\": 1792894272440177000, \"started_ns\": 1792894272439662000}, \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.observation/1\", \"scope\": [{\"kind\": \"file\", \"path\": \"build_tenants/codex/README.md\", \"root\": \"product\"}, {\"kind\": \"file\", \"path\": \"build_tenants/codex/tests/verify_package.py\", \"root\": \"product\"}]}}, \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.response/1\", \"status\": \"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json, subprocess, pathlib, hashlib, sys, time\nargv=json.loads(\\\"[\\\\\\\"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-B\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--policy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/successor-1/codex/worker-policy.json\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--policy-sha256\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"038f1b1fdd56d0860dbfc94a0a17ff28e98e41153f6774cf4dc5ff7658d425b9\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--principal\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"codex\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"--request\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\"]\\\")\ntask=json.loads(\\\"{\\\\\\\"engine\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"root\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"successor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"codex/TASK.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"sha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"4c33deea408deef15ac9900f66d5986b06efefb94de40697cf249d536770845b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"selector\\\\\\\":null}\\\")\nroot=pathlib.Path(\\\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills\\\")\ndef call(op,args,rid):\n r=subprocess.run(argv,input=json.dumps({\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":rid,\\\"operation\\\":op,\\\"arguments\\\":args}),text=True,capture_output=True)\n if r.returncode or r.stderr:\n  print(json.dumps({\\\"transport_exit\\\":r.returncode,\\\"stderr\\\":r.stderr}),flush=True)\n result=json.loads(r.stdout)\n if result[\\\"status\\\"]\"'!=\"ok\":\n  print(json.dumps(result),flush=True); raise SystemExit(\"Required public operation failed; no retry\")\n return result\n\ndef write(rel,content,rid):\n p=root/rel\n allowed=[root/\"build_tenants/codex\",root/\".ai-workspace/work/T001/codex/actor/successor-1\"]\n if not any(p.is_relative_to(a) for a in allowed) or \"..\" in pathlib.PurePath(rel).parts: raise SystemExit(\"territory escape\")\n for ancestor in [p,*p.parents]:\n  if ancestor.is_symlink(): raise SystemExit(\"symlink refused: \"+str(ancestor))\n p.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n before=call(\"workspace.observe\",{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":str(p.parent.relative_to(root)),\"kind\":\"directory\"}]},rid+\"-observe\")\n pre=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() if p.exists() else None\n target={\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":rel,\"object\":None,\"sha256\":pre,\"selector\":None}\n result=call(\"work.write\",{\"grant_id\":\"urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:2\",\"target\":target,\"mode\":\"replace\",\"record\":{\"text\":content,\"provenance\":task},\"interpretation\":None,\"observations\":[before[\"result\"][\"artifact\"]]},rid)\n print(json.dumps({\"path\":rel,\"observation\":before[\"result\"][\"artifact\"],\"evidence\":result[\"evidence\"],\"result_artifact\":result[\"result\"][\"artifact\"],\"value\":{k:v for k,v in result[\"result\"][\"value\"].items() if k not in [\"record\",\"interpretation\"]},\"operation_outcome\":result[\"operation_outcome\"]}),flush=True)\n return result\n\nfiles=json.loads(\"{'\"\\\\\\\"skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"---\\\\\\\\nname: stdo-work\\\\\\\\ndescription: Apply a selected STDO method to governed software work, including setup, scoped changes, independent review, recovery and release preparation. Use for tasks in an STDO workspace or explicit STDO setup; do not impose STDO on unrelated requests.\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# STDO work\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nHelp the user complete the requested work under the selected Product and exact method. This package targets STDO v3.0.1-rc.1; its manifest and source routes are in [basis](references/basis.md). It supplies instructions, not authority.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Identify the outcome and changed owner: requirement, design, implementation, assessment or release. Select exactly one applicable Product Definition, or an explicitly authorized cross-Product relation. Read the applicable local bootstrap and deciding sources. If an activated Context already supplies the exact binding, use it and acquire only its missing material sources.\\\\\\\\n2. Verify the pinned installation and operation compatibility through [basis](references/basis.md) and [tools](references/tools.md). Preserve sufficient existing authorization. Ask only for a material missing decision, not repeated consent for already granted work.\\\\\\\\n3. Choose the smallest sufficient path. For an authorized one-file correction with adequate requirement/design, enter the bound direct Writer path: acquire current preimage, make only that effect through its declared tool, perform focused proof and return to its consumer. Do not require a new ticket, Executive or independent reviewer solely because work exists.\\\\\\\\n4. Use [delegation](references/delegation.md) when a material context, capability, ownership or required independence boundary calls for it. An Executive coordinates without mutating; a separately granted Worker/Writer implements. Do not launch actors unless the current grant permits them.\\\\\\\\n5. Make the requested change and inspect actual responses and postimages. Read [recovery](references/recovery.md) on continuation, interruption, refusal or stale evidence. An unsupported required tool withholds the dependent claim. An uncertain effect must be reconciled before repeating it.\\\\\\\\n6. Return the exact candidate, source/basis identities, actual proof, failures, remaining obligations and invalidators. Keep availability, author assessment, independent review and owner acceptance separate. For release/install work use [release and installation](references/release-install.md); for behavior qualification use [qualification](references/qualification.md).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNormal invocation: ask for the relevant task in a governed workspace. Explicit invocation: \"'`$stdo-work Correct the named file under the existing grant`. The host may discover the description automatically; acquisition and success must be observed separately. If explicit invocation works after failed automatic discovery, retain both attempts.'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRead only the reference needed for the current branch. Common requirements and method owners remain external authority; [source routes](source-routes.json) identify this package's construction basis. A target workspace supplies its own Product Definition, sources and grants.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# Bind the exact workspace and method\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRun the manager on the selected target Product Definition, not this package's construction definition by default:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\"'```sh'\"\\\\\\\\nstdo status --definition /absolute/path/to/selected-product.json --verify\\\\\\\\n\"'```'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nInspect the actual result: installed, valid, failures, definition identity, basis, manifest and installed path. This candidate supports exactly \"'`stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`. A channel is discovery, never adoption. Missing install, changed member, ambiguous Product or another cut withholds dependent work; name the missing premise and its owner. Setup may install/pin only where its operation grant permits, using the manager'\"'s discovered supported contract. Do not guess a setup command.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nResolve the definition's declared bootstrap from the verified installed path. For an already activated step, do not reload the whole method. Acquire the deciding sections for the task through the selected source.read contract. [Source routes](../source-routes.json) retain exact common/host/tool provenance for this package; root names are resolved by the active policy, not silently rebound to a sibling.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| Decision | Owner in the exact installation's standards directory |\\\\\\\\n|---|---|\\\\\\\\n| Product selection and install | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\\\\\\\\n| WHAT/HOW and tenant | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\\\\\\\\n| Intake, existing authority and admission | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\\\\\\\\n| Bounded context and exact activation | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\\\\\\\\n| Result and effect | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\\\\\\\\n| Executive/Worker roles | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\\\\\\\\n| Independent review | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\\\\\\\\n| Recovery/currentness | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\\\\\\\\n| Proportional proof | ACTIVATION.md §6 and transition evidence |\\\\\\\\n| Actual path | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\\\\\\\\n| Release/adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThese are routes, not copied law. Use the manager's verified member hashes and exact SourceRefs; select the needed lines only after locating the section in that member. Read changed-owner source before changing realization. Preserve higher meaning unless its owner actually authorizes change. The package cannot adopt or repair its immutable method.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRecord the relevant host version, resolved model/effort when observable, tool implementation and method profile. HOST.md identifies codex-cli 0.164.0 mechanics for this candidate; it does not prove any run's resolved model. Missing usage/model evidence remains unknown.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# Public tool path\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUse the operation implementation selected by the target Product/activation. The construction binding is \"'`urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256 `a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`. Its legacy builder identity is separate. Native results.conjoin is unsupported; never relabel a legacy conjunction.'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe ordinary public CLI is sufficient. Supply an exact policy, its digest and the authorized principal; inherit the environment. For this construction the observed executable is Python 3.13.7 and the entrypoint is \"'`/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py`. Resolve that development-tool installation explicitly in another workspace. Do not assume a portable absolute path.'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis executable transport pattern reads an envelope from stdin, creates no request file and preserves the CLI's response:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\"'```sh'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\"'$AC_PYTHON'\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -B \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\"'$AC_ENTRY'\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --policy \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\"'$AC_POLICY'\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --policy-sha256 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\"'$AC_POLICY_SHA256'\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --principal \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\"'$AC_PRINCIPAL'\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  call --request - <<'JSON'\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"describe-work-write-unique\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"operation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tools.describe\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"operation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"work.write\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\nJSON\\\\\\\\n\"'```'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSet AC_PYTHON, AC_ENTRY, AC_POLICY, AC_POLICY_SHA256 and AC_PRINCIPAL from the active tool binding, not example authority. Use a distinct request id for each new operation. Reuse acquired schemas while their basis is current. Inspect status, refusal, result, operation_outcome and evidence. Save actual responses through the authorized evidence mechanism; a successful process exit is not a semantic verdict.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAcquisition envelope arguments:\\\\\\\\n\"'```json'\"\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"engine\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"root\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"method\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sha256\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"selector\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lines\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[1004,1055]}},\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"encoding\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"utf8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\n\"'```'\"\\\\\\\\nUse operation \"'`source.read` in the same envelope. Root aliases and access must exist in the selected policy. Preserve parent/selected digests and acquisition evidence.'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor an authorized write:\\\\\\\\n1. Ensure the containing directory exists through an explicitly granted mechanism. If mkdir is allowed, reject symlinks and path escape. No directory permission can be inferred from file permission.\\\\\\\\n2. Call \"'`workspace.observe` with `{'\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"root\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"product\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"the/containing/directory\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"directory\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}\"'`. Retain its result.artifact; do not substitute the response evidence for the observation.'\"\\\\\\\\n3. Call \"'`work.write` using the exact returned input schema: grant_id; target SourceRef with exact preimage digest (null only when absent); mode '\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"replace\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" or the granted append; record {text, provenance}; interpretation null unless declared; observations [the fresh observation artifact]. Provenance is the actual authority source.\\\\\\\\n4. Retain the returned postimage, effect scope, result artifact and OperationEvidence. Check that the postimage matches intended bytes. No further dependent effect after uncertainty until reconciliation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor \"'`evidence.read`, arguments are `{'\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"artifact\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sha256:…\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sha256\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"…\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\"'`; supply the real returned digest. The ellipsis here denotes a required observed value, not an executable request.'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor context, admission, review or dispatch use \"'`tools.describe` for the named operation and current method_profile, then construct its exact input from the active contract. Discovery is not authority. If the required operation or binding is unsupported, preserve the real refusal and return the required capability/owner; do not invoke a substitute and claim the original path passed. An F_P assessment is authored evidence, not a deterministic tool predicate. Native Executive consumption must retain all required evaluations, applicability uncertainty, incompatible bases and contradictions; it cannot fabricate a qualified join.'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAuxiliary host reads/hashes/read-only validators establish finite byte facts only. Any host mutation requires its own declared operation grant and actual-path qualification; it never stands in for a required tool result.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"skills/stdo-work/references/delegation.md\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# Bounded handoff and independent review\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUse delegation only when required by a material boundary and authorized by the current configuration. A sufficient direct Writer task goes straight from current basis/grant to the exact effect and focused proof; no automatic coordination or review gate is added.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBefore handoff retain:\\\\\\\\n- Exact outcome and subject; Product Definition and immutable method; governing requirement and design; changed producer, transport, consumer and artifact relations.\\\\\\\\n- Frame id/revision and result algebra; activation identity; operation grant and precise territory; separate semantic, evaluation, decision, acceptance and publication authorities.\\\\\\\\n- Required evidence and predicates; admissible source routes; retained failures/counterexamples; original observations and their provenance.\\\\\\\\n- Host/tool implementation and method support; actor/context/resource limits and exclusions; stop/change invalidators; return schema and named consumer.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSelect only the smallest dependency-ready reference frontier that preserves those distinctions. If it does not fit the envelope, refine or sequence within existing authority; seek the actual missing capability or envelope decision when needed. Do not erase material obligations to fit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDiscover the supported \"'`context.assemble`, `contract.preflight`, `dispatch.start`, `dispatch.observe`, `return.capture` and `return.check` contracts through the public path in [tools](tools.md), selecting only operations required by this activation. A missing supported binding stops the dependent handoff. Do not replace the selected dispatch with a native spawn just because it exists. Retain the actual input delivery, process result, stdout/stderr and parsed original closed return. Transport success and actor output availability do not establish requested effects or fitness.'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nWorkers implement only their grant, self-assess the exact candidate and return. They do not activate the next stage. Executive consumes closed results and selects only an already authorized next action; if a record must be written, bind a Writer rather than mutating in the Executive frame.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nA required Reviewer acquires governing sources and derives expected behavior before the exact candidate and proof. Use a fresh permitted reviewer and retain actual exposure, author relationship, model family/resolution and limitations. Nonauthor same-family review does not prove cross-family independence. Where a review.prepare tool is selected, actually call its supported contract. The Reviewer reports findings, severity, evidence, affected claims and uncertainty; it does not implement the adopted repair or decide promotion. After material repair, withdraw only affected old reliance and obtain the required fresh assessment.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nA returned candidate_ready concerns availability. Assessments keep their own predicates and results. Owner disposition is a separate act. Contradictory results require disposition, not majority voting.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"skills/stdo-work/references/recovery.md\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# Resume from evidence\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nOn restart acquire the current target, material governing sources, grant, operation records and retained return/effect evidence. Preserve their original identities and distinguish historical acquisition from fresh observation. Compare the changed inputs and apply only affected invalidators.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor identical candidate bytes with different histories, do not produce the same continuation automatically:\\\\\\\\n- A current applicable accepted assessment may support the next already authorized action.\\\\\\\\n- An unresolved counterexample that defeats that assessment withholds the dependent claim. Preserve the obligation, reacquire its deciding source, and route to the required repair or reassessment owner. Equal file hashes cannot erase it.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAfter a timeout or lost acknowledgment:\\\\\\\\n1. Retain the original request/attempt id and unknown-effect state. Do not resend it or infer rollback.\\\\\\\\n2. Acquire a new workspace.observe of the target and read the original operation/effect evidence with evidence.read.\\\\\\\\n3. If intended postimage and qualified completion evidence agree, consume that single effect without repeating it.\\\\\\\\n4. If only changed bytes are visible, establish their custody and intended-effect relation; unrelated matching bytes alone do not close it. If absence is established, retry only through the declared recovery contract and existing authority. Otherwise return the unreconciled effect and missing observation. Process end alone does not prove descendant/external end.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor unsupported method, execution error or missing acquisition retain the actual refusal/error. Withhold dependent success, name the precise re-entry (tool owner, basis owner or operation owner), and preserve useful partial artifacts. Continue only independent authorized work. Do not silently switch tools or repeat an uncertain effect.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUse the selected return contract. Under this native binding:\\\\\\\\n- candidate_ready: exact candidate plus transition evidence exists; not a fitness result.\\\\\\\\n- incomplete: activated construction ended without its needed output; its availability is falsified, with stop cause and residuals.\\\\\\\\n- refused: an applicable prohibition or owner-valid refusal defeats construction.\\\\\\\\n- re_entry_requested: name basis or authority cause; map materially unusable basis to invalid_basis and missing authority to out_of_frame.\\\\\\\\n- A performed assessment returns satisfied, falsified with counterexample, indeterminate on undecidable admissible evidence, invalid_basis, or out_of_frame as warranted.\\\\\\\\n- An unperformed assessment has no result and belongs in not_performed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nClose with original frame, activation, subject, method/observation basis, actor and consumer. Add exact current artifact/effect evidence without replacing the original activation basis. Retain failed attempts and unknown costs. After source/tool/host/grant/candidate changes or a counterexample, invalidate only affected reliance with its cause and preserve unrelated valid evidence. Never declare acceptance from test totals.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"skills/stdo-work/references/release-install.md\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# Release preparation and scoped deployment\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAcquire RELEASE.md and IDENTITY.md from the verified installation and the target Product's release conditions. Bind exact candidate inventory, evidence, acceptance/disposition requirements, destination and publication grant. With a preparation-only grant, assemble a reviewable local artifact and return it; no remote publication follows. Do not invent a second final cut to fix an identity problem. Discover and actually use the release tool contract selected by that Product; unsupported release tooling leaves publication unperformed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis skill's deployment unit is the entire stdo-work directory. Its repository-local destination is exactly TARGET/.agents/skills/stdo-work. It neither installs the Claude tenant nor modifies host defaults. The tenant README documents the executable package verifier and copy recipe. At deployment time:\\\\\\\\n1. Freeze the package inventory, verify all ordinary regular files and internal resources, and retain the chosen identity outside the discovery directory.\\\\\\\\n2. Verify the target grant and every destination ancestor: no symlink, escape or unexpected existing stdo-work. Resolve duplicate skill names deliberately; names are not merged.\\\\\\\\n3. Install only that directory. Record destination, exact file inventory and old/new package identities in the authorized work surface.\\\\\\\\n4. Open Codex in that workspace. Exercise ordinary discovery and explicit \"'$stdo-work invocation as separate trials. Confirm acquisition and required tool events. If stale, restart and retain the failed discovery attempt.'\"\\\\\\\\n5. For update, compare the entire installed file set and hashes to the retained old receipt before replacement. If locally changed or ownership unknown, stop that replacement and report the conflict; do not overwrite it. Retain the old package outside all discovery roots and its identity for deliberate rollback.\\\\\\\\n6. Remove only the owned selected stdo-work directory after the same receipt check. Preserve .agents/skills, other skills and configuration. Unknown files or hashes block destructive removal. Recheck the remaining unrelated configuration.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThese instructions specify a deployable path. Finite package checks do not prove discovery, actual installation, update or removal behavior; Q12 remains open until performed in an authorized disposable host workspace. Installation does not constitute method adoption or Product acceptance.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"skills/stdo-work/references/qualification.md\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# Qualification boundary\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nCommon requirements and scenarios remain exact external authority in [source routes](../source-routes.json). Derive expected outcomes independently before acquiring the tenant answer. Freeze an isolated workspace, exact source/package/tool/method cuts, authority, host/model/settings, input exposure, time/resource bound and lane. Automatic discovery and explicit invocation are separate attempts; a fallback never erases an automatic failure.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| Required case | Evidence needed; current construction standing |\\\\\\\\n|---|---|\\\\\\\\n| Q01 | Ordinary request discovers skill and performs bounded tool-backed change; fresh explicit lane; actual host unperformed |\\\\\\\\n| Q02 | Unrelated task avoids forced STDO setup; actual host unperformed |\\\\\\\\n| Q03 | Valid pin and missing/altered/ambiguous variants; actual host variants unperformed |\\\\\\\\n| Q04 | Sufficient one-file direct Writer uses focused proof without invented ticket/coordination/review; author walkthrough only |\\\\\\\\n| Q05 | Actual worker handoff and source-first independent reviewer; unperformed |\\\\\\\\n| Q06 | Actual unsupported/error response retained and dependent success withheld; host trials unperformed |\\\\\\\\n| Q07 | Equal bytes with accepted history versus unresolved counterexample cause distinct continuation; author walkthrough only |\\\\\\\\n| Q08 | Changed target with lost acknowledgment reconciled before retry; host trial unperformed |\\\\\\\\n| Q09 | Material source/candidate change withdraws affected review reliance only; unperformed |\\\\\\\\n| Q10 | Incomplete availability, inconclusive assessment and unperformed assessment remain distinct; unperformed |\\\\\\\\n| Q11 | Preparation-only authority and separately authorized local deployment; unperformed |\\\\\\\\n| Q12 | Scoped install/invoke/update/remove with resource and unrelated-config checks; unperformed |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRetain each actual invocation, input delivery, source acquisition, output, tool trace, effect/postimage, per-predicate verdict and counterexample, residual and invalidator. Measure elapsed time and reported tokens/cost; unavailable data stays unknown. Include retries, repair and review in total cost and compare equivalent substantive information. One successful trial is bounded evidence, not a reliability estimate or general efficiency benefit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRun the cheapest focused check capable of falsifying the current change; expensive whole-candidate host qualification belongs at its declared boundary. The read-only package verifier checks actual metadata, resource containment and file inventory. It does not grade semantic success by keywords. Author instruction assessment must separately inspect the actual bodies and reason through Q04, Q07 and Q06/Q08. Independent review and all mandatory host cases remain necessary for initial delivery; construction cannot silently waive them.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nHost/tool/method or prompt changes identify affected trials and claims. Retain unaffected evidence with a justified currentness relation. Tune from observed failures rather than accumulating universal process.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"skills/stdo-work/source-routes.json\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"stdo-skills.codex.source-routes/1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"standing\\\\\\\